			"Message": "fix(Maintain): Correct escape sequences in Dependency.sh for consistency\n\nSigned-off-by: Nikola Hristov <Nikola@PlayForm.Cloud>",
			"SHA": "0b02d19a5dd69b924acf48322965b1fbb2d38a2f"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-19T19:00:48Z",
			"File": [
				"⣿⡇⠀⠀⠀",
				176,
				54
			],
			"Message": "chore(Maintain): Refactor shell scripts with explicit command prefixes and add dependency synchronization utilities\n\nStandardize the `Maintain` directory shell scripts by prefixing all built-in commands and external binaries with explicit backslashes (e.g., `\\echo`, `\\cd`, `\\pwd`) to enforce strict path resolution and prevent accidental execution of shadowed aliases. This applies to the core dependency management suite including `Append`, `Clean`, `Clone`, `Configure`, `Move`, `Rename`, `Restore`, and `Sync` operations.\n\nIntroduce `Maintain/Pull/Dependency.sh` to automate merging upstream changes from the `Parent` remote into the `Current` branch for dependency forks. This script handles fast-forward merges and staged merges with automatic conflict resolution for build artifacts (lock files, `node_modules`), allowing developers to review and commit changes manually. Also add `Maintain/Pull/Tauri.sh` to manage upstream synchronization specifically for Tauri ecosystem sub-dependencies referenced in `Land/Cargo.toml`.\n\nUpdate `Maintain/Restore/History` scripts to utilize the new explicit command prefixes for robust execution when restoring specific file states from upstream repositories.\n\nThese changes improve the reliability of the dependency synchronization pipeline and enforce a consistent execution model across all maintenance tools.",
			"SHA": "efe5112284b0c47f62fa605dcaa6909ba9a49fbc"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-14T16:34:19Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				171,
				2
			],
			"Message": "build(Deps): Sync Editor to 0a610158 and streamline build docs\n\nUpdate the VS Code Editor dependency submodule (Microsoft) from 66809e46 to 0a610158 to integrate critical stability improvements for the Agent Host Phase 9 lifecycle. Key upstream changes include robust runtime mutation for live sessions (abort, model hot-swapping, steering), subprocess crash recovery without fatal latches, and fixed terminal trust checks.\n\nConcurrently, refactor the root `README.md` to remove verbose, inline build instructions. Redirect users to the centralized `Documentation/GitHub/Building.md` to maintain a cleaner repository overview while referencing the `Dependency` element's role in housing third-party sources.\n\nThis ensures the Cocoon extension host and Mountain backend leverage the latest upstream stability fixes while reducing documentation maintenance overhead in the root directory.",
			"SHA": "05f43861314ead03ada2a37a22bd31d5a39ff934"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-14T01:30:47Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				171,
				1
			],
			"Message": "sync(Deps/Editor): Update to 66809e46 with Agent Host Phase 9 crash recovery\n\nSynchronize the VS Code Editor dependency submodule from 900a349 to 66809e46 to integrate critical stability improvements and advanced agent capabilities required for the Cocoon extension host and Mountain backend.\n\nKey upstream changes include:\n- **Agent Host Phase 9:** Implemented robust runtime mutation for live sessions, enabling abort, model hot-swapping, and steering. Added crash recovery mechanisms that prevent permanent fatal latches, allowing subprocess restarts and state replay.\n- **Terminal Reliability:** Fixed background terminal accumulation issues and enforced strict trust checks for local terminals within remote workspaces.\n- **Bug Fixes:** Resolved null guards in configuration trees, corrected off-by-one errors in extension pagination, and fixed protected modifier visibility.\n- **UI Enhancements:** Enabled output renderers for chat code blocks and improved markdown frontmatter rendering.\n\nThis update ensures the editor maintains stability during complex agent operations and prevents indefinite hangs or UI corruption during extension lifecycle events.\n\nRefs: microsoft/vscode",
			"SHA": "fb4e9e7ab7317d0cff67d63eac2c4a2193dae443"
		}
	],
